  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Programme pilote pour l&apos;education des filles (PPEF)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To pilot approaches on girls education. Education is recognized as a fundamental right in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC). However, despite the launch of a free basic education policy in 2019 many Congolese children are still unable to access education. This programme directly contributes to the Prime Minister&#x2019;s commitment to 12 years of quality education for girls and the Strategic Framework for ODA&#x2019;s global commitment to get 40 million girls into education and 20 million more girls reading by the age of 10.</narrative>
  </description>
